            view: "**Capacity nearly tripling, but the profit is not arriving as cash.** Operating cash was ₹33cr against ₹85cr of profit over FY22–FY26 (39%), and −₹14cr against ₹41cr of profit in FY26; ₹115cr of bills are discounted off the balance sheet, the auditor flagged unconfirmed balances, and on 5 Nov 2026 it closed a QIP of 1.20 crore shares at ₹125 (about ₹150cr, about 10% dilution, below the ₹155 market price). Q1 earned a record ₹10,401 a tonne with the margin back to 11%, and guidance is ₹1,300–1,350cr this year against ₹884cr in FY26. The price asks for about my ~20% estimate; it returns to follow when operating cash turns positive and covers most of its profit. 6 Nov 2026: filed Q2 revenue rose 45% at a 10.7% margin, close to the 11% guided; the call transcript, and so the cash figures, are not out yet.",
            watch: 'The second paint line at 50–60% in H2; operating cash turning positive and discounted bills falling; how the ₹150cr QIP money and the rest of phase 2 are spent; the ₹210cr European export MoU (5 Nov 2026) turning into orders.',
