    closing: {
        heading: '9. Summary review',
        body: [
            "**Integrated steel makers.** **Shyam Metalics: follow.** The largest company here, with a strong balance sheet and a price that fits my estimate, but a cyclical business with ₹10,041cr of plants to build, four years of negative free cash and an ED attachment the auditor highlights. **Sambhv Steel Tubes: follow.** A low-cost maker beating its own guidance, but its Kesda stainless plant must arrive on time while debt roughly trebles, and the promoters' warrants are cheap.",
            "**Carbon-steel pipe and coated sheet.** **Man Industries: follow.** One of the best cash records here, a cheap Saudi purchase and Aramco approval, but guidance at the low end, debt rising to about ₹1,600cr and a governance record that deserves a discount. **Maharashtra Seamless: follow.** The cheapest price here, with net cash about half its market value and 55% of Indian seamless pipe, but treasury income is 41% of pre-tax profit, the Chinese-pipe duty needs renewing by January and the new demerger does not yet say who gets the cash. **Manaksia Coated Metals: wait.** The price fits and the new line should lift earnings, but operating cash was ₹33cr against ₹85cr of profit over five years (−₹14cr in FY26), so it returns to follow only when operating cash turns positive and covers most of its profit.",
            "**Stainless-steel pipes, tubes, bars, hoses and fasteners.** **Ratnamani Metals: wait.** The best franchise in stainless tube, with net cash and a record spool order, but standalone sales fell 30% in Q1, the Saudi plant slipped a year and the price assumes a recovery. **Scoda Tubes: wait.** A modest price, but a little more than I now expect, until its cash cycle falls back below CARE's trigger and it hits a target. **Venus Pipes: wait** until profit grows with revenue and the share issue settles. **Aeroflex: wait.** A real data-centre business, priced for years of it. **Welspun Specialty: pass.** Rare nuclear and boiler-tube approvals, but a 5% margin, falling volume and a price that needs about {need:Welspun Specialty|35}% a year. **Ratnaveer Precision: avoid.** Capitalised costs equal to half its operating profit, negative free cash every year, equity raised every year and a laminate bet it has never made.",
            "**Special steel, wire and wire rope.** **Usha Martin: follow.** India's dominant rope maker with a 20% margin, net cash and an upgrade, but flat tonnes and ED and CBI cases in the auditor's report. **Vardhman Special Steels: follow.** Well run, with Aichi Steel behind it and net cash, but sold out until an environmental approval arrives and a large equity raise is coming. **Bharat Wire Ropes: wait.** Debt cut and the price looks low, but sales are flat, a third of operating profit is state subsidy, half the promoter stake is pledged and ₹383cr of lender-held preference shares can turn into equity.",
            "**Engineered steel products.** **Technocraft Industries: follow.** The price fits and drum closures are a gem, but Q1 leaned on the rupee and investment gains, textiles earn nothing and the cash cycle is 306 days; own it if profit holds near ₹100cr a quarter. **Goodluck India: wait.** Defence shells are lifting profit, but free cash has been negative for four years and the swap ratio for folding in the defence subsidiary will decide what listed holders get. **Shivalik Bimetal: wait.** A real niche at a 24% margin, but the core grew 13%, the CFO is leaving and the price needs about {need:Shivalik Bimetal|26}% a year.",
            "**What would change my view.** For the better: the ED attachment on Shyam's subsidiary lifted and its free cash turning positive; Kesda's equipment going in on schedule; NPC running at ₹300–500cr a quarter with Man's margin at 14% or more; Manaksia's operating cash turning positive; Aeroflex winning a second skid customer; Venus's margin above 17%. Among the newer names: Maharashtra Seamless's duty renewed and a demerger that leaves the cash with all shareholders; Ratnamani's standalone sales back above ₹1,100cr a quarter; Usha Martin's tonnes growing and its ED and CBI cases closed; Vardhman's environmental approval; Technocraft's profit holding near ₹100cr a quarter; a fair merger ratio at Goodluck; a plan for Bharat Wire's preference shares; and two years of positive operating cash at Ratnaveer. For the worse: carbon-steel prices falling as new mill capacity arrives; Kesda slipping into FY28 as cheaper Chinese stainless coil returns; a tribunal loss for Man's chairman and MD; Saudi pipe prices falling as new capacity arrives; the EU tightening its quota further; a rating cut for Scoda. Among the newer names: the seamless-pipe duty lapsing; US dumping duties on Indian welded stainless pipe; a CBI conviction at Usha Martin; Vardhman's approval refused; the rupee strengthening sharply for Technocraft; Goodluck's merger diluting listed holders; and the state incentive at Bharat Wire delayed.",
            "**What to watch next quarter.** Shyam's volumes, capex spend and the ED case; Sambhv's Kesda progress and profit a tonne; Man's Saudi revenue and debt; Manaksia's paint line and cash; Aeroflex's skid capacity; Venus's share-issue vote and spool start; Scoda's welded plant and half-year cash flow. Among the newer names: the Maharashtra Seamless demerger terms and duty review; Ratnamani's standalone sales and spool billing; Usha Martin's rope tonnes; Vardhman's environmental approval and equity raise; Technocraft's profit without the rupee; Goodluck's merger ratio and shell expansion; Bharat Wire's volume and preference-share plan; Shivalik's core growth and new CFO; Welspun Specialty's volumes; and Ratnaveer's capitalised costs and laminate start-up.",
        ],
        bottomLine:
            "No company here is a clear buy today. Follow Shyam Metalics and Technocraft, where the prices fit but the latest profit is cyclical or flattered; Usha Martin, Man Industries, Maharashtra Seamless, Vardhman Special Steels and Sambhv Steel Tubes, each strong in its niche but with a full price, a governance question or a project still to prove. Wait on Manaksia Coated Metals and Goodluck India until profit arrives as cash, on Ratnamani Metals, Shivalik Bimetal, Venus Pipes and Aeroflex Industries until their price catches up with their growth, and on Scoda Tubes and Bharat Wire Ropes until they meet a target. Pass on Welspun Specialty and avoid Ratnaveer Precision.",
    },

